Qt for Python 6.11.2 is a bug-fix release.

For more details, refer to the online documentation included in this
distribution. The documentation is also available online:

https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython/

Some of the changes listed in this file include issue tracking numbers
corresponding to tasks in the Qt Bug Tracker:

https://bugreports.qt.io/

Each of these identifiers can be entered in the bug tracker to obtain more
information about a particular change.

****************************************************************************
*                                  PySide6                                 *
****************************************************************************

 - [PYSIDE-1612] pyside6-project: Options for deployment have been added.
 - [PYSIDE-1612] Deployment: Nuitka has been updated to 4.1.1.
 - [PYSIDE-2206] The buildings part of the OSM buildings demo has been added.
 - [PYSIDE-2541] Type hints: The QML decorators type hint has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3168] Class QCanvasGradientStop has been added.
 - [PYSIDE-3203] Type hints: QSplitter.replaceWidget() has been fixed
                 to return optional.
 - [PYSIDE-3301] The colorpaletteclient example has been updated
                 and a small server has been added.
 - [PYSIDE-3311] pyside6-project/qmltyperegistrar: Empty .qmltypes files
                 have been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3339] Type hints: The return type of QObject.parent() has been
                 fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3347] Documentation: The module index pages have been updated
                 and some security-relevant documentation has been added.
 - [PYSIDE-3353] A crash calling a class method, such as QObject::tr()
                 using the snake case feature has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3356] Exception handling in QCoreApplication.processEvents()
                 has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3360] metaobjectdump: Decorated Python enum classes are now
                 recognized.
 - [PYSIDE-3380] A crash using QAction.menu() has been fixed.
 - [PYSIDE-3406] Support for developer versions of libclang with
                 non-standard values of LLVM_PACKAGE_VERSION has been
                 improved.

****************************************************************************
*                                  Shiboken6                               *
****************************************************************************

 - [PYSIDE-3308] User-added global functions can now also be marked as
                 deprecated.
 - [PYSIDE-3365] The formatting of children/referenced objects in
                 Shiboken6.dump() has been  improved.
